Hi Enrique,

> When roxygen founds a replacement method like "[<-.XXX", it tries to 
> write to disk a file named "[<-.XXX.Rd", which fails on windows as "<" 
> is not an accepted character in filenames. Is there a solution or 
> workaround?

You can set a name with the @name tag; then this is used as
filename. And if you want, set "[<-" as an @alias tag.


Manuel.

